  "rationale": "structural: The only structural obligation in `requirements.sdk.graph.validation-context.ValidationContext.dependencies` is the prescribed signature: an inherent method `pub fn dependencies(&self) -> Vec<Dependency<NodeId<D>, D::EdgeLabel>>` on `impl<'d, D: Domain> ValidationContext<'d, D>`. A method that took `self` by value or returned a different type would break that signature, so the signature is binding. The root `crates/trust-but-verify/src/procedure.rs#impl[ValidationContext<'d, D>]#2/fn[dependencies]` declares exactly that signature and carries the `{impl}` marker. It locks `self.observations` and returns `.clone()`, which is a snapshot (an owned `Vec`). The field `struct[ValidationContext]` `observations` is a `Mutex<Vec<Dependency<NodeId<D>, D::EdgeLabel>>>`. `record_read` and `observe_edges_by` push into that same vector, so reads made after the snapshot still contribute to the execution. That continuing-contribution clause describes observable behavior, and no particular structure is required for it. Behavior tests can cover it. The root needs no further markers.\n\nbehavioral: The requirement has two behavioral obligations: `dependencies()` returns a snapshot of the observations collected so far, and later reads keep contributing to the execution. `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph/validation_tests.rs#fn[snapshots_record_exact_reads_and_retain_distinct_versions]` covers both.\n\n- **Empty start:** it asserts `dependencies()` is empty on a fresh context.\n- **Snapshot of reads so far:** after one `read` it captures `earlier` and checks that it equals `[Node(1, fp(\"before\"))]`.\n- **Snapshot stays fixed:** after the content changes and further reads happen, it asserts `earlier` is unchanged. This shows the returned value is an independent snapshot.\n- **Later reads contribute:** it asserts that a later `read` of the changed content adds `Node(1, fp(\"after\"))`. The final `dependencies()` is `[before, after]`.\n- **Failed read:** it asserts that a failed read of node 2 adds nothing.\n- **Record:** the `finish` record carries the same dependencies.\n\nEdge observations (`Dependency::OutgoingEdges`) go into the same `observations` vector. The implementation, `crates/trust-but-verify/src/procedure.rs#impl[ValidationContext<'d, D>]#2/fn[dependencies]`, returns that vector's clone and has no conditional or transformation of its own. Other tests in `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/configured.rs` also assert edge entries in `cx.dependencies()`. Edge recording belongs to other requirements, so no extra test is needed here.\n\n`crates/trust-but-verify/tests/public_api.rs#fn[public_exports_match_the_appendix]` checks the exported signature. It adds no behavioral obligation.",
